# Isolith CODEOWNERS
#
# Review policy record for P0-M1-T04 (contributor rules) as extended by the
# PUBLIC-REPO-HARDENING baseline: one owner row per Cargo workspace
# workstream plus the governance directories, a catch-all default so nothing
# falls between rows, and explicit rows for the release lane, the governance
# records and the brand assets.
#
# Dual syntax, because two hosts read this file:
#   - the internal Gitea mirror parses each pattern as a Go regexp and the
#     P0-M1-T04 acceptance test pins those rows ('.*' catch-all and the
#     'crates/<name>/.*' per-workstream rows);
#   - the public GitHub primary parses gitignore globs, so each pinned row
#     has a GitHub twin (catch-all '*' and 'crates/<name>/' directory rows)
#     plus explicit rows for release, governance and brand coverage.
# GitHub resolves the most specific pattern for a path; today every row
# resolves to the same maintainer (see GOVERNANCE.md), and a workstream lead
# slots in by adding their handle to their rows.
#
# Team dependency: @isolith/Owners references the Owners team under the
# Isolith account or org the owner names (GATE-PUBLIC-SURFACE,
# GITHUB-PRIMARY-MIGRATION). Until it exists this is a forward declaration.

# Catch-all defaults: Gitea regexp (.+) and GitHub glob (*).
.* @isolith/Owners
* @isolith/Owners

# Governance records (GitHub primary).
